{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1212010-enlightened-programming","id":1212010,"title":"Enlightened Programming","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-04-26T15:16:49-07:00","id":1212010,"title":"Enlightened Programming","content":"Computers, hacking, programming and gaming... they're a big deal in the consensus these days, and they are only augmented by Hollywood Reality. Some people, as a result, are able to exploit the incredible power granted to computing by the consensus and master Enlightened Programming.<br /> <br /> EP is a separate Knowledge from Computer, however your EP rating cannot exceed your Computer rating (as with Hyper-tech and Technology).<br /> <br /> EP is to Computer what Do is to Martial Arts and Brawl; it grants some innate benefits, and comes with unique options which are only just possible because of the way the consensus understands computing.<br /> <br /> - Well Trained Advantage. If you are a practitioner of EP, you make mundane Computer rolls (that is, no Arete or EP maneuvers) at -1 difficulty, since they are relatively simple and more &quot;Real&quot; than the advanced programming you have struggled to comprehend.<br /> <br /> - EP comes with a list of &quot;believable but impossible&quot; computing maneuvers. These are not Magick, in the same way that Do is not Magick. And just as an enlightened understanding of martial arts can grant a sleeper seemingly supernatural abilities, EP can give hackers &quot;Hollywood Hacker&quot; powers. One maneuver may be learned for every dot you gain in EP beyond the first.<br /> <br /> - Internet Stardom.<br /> <br /> This maneuver generally gives you more of an allure and a presence in online spaces. Exploiting the the coincidental concept of certain people shining in online spaces (.com billionaires, multi-media millionaires with millions of followers, net wisdom gurus) means that your social rolls in digital spaces gain an extra die for every dot you have in EP. For example, a Charisma + Expression roll made while creating a youtube video or forum post would gain a dice bonus from EP.<br /> <br /> - Van Eck Input.<br /> <br /> It finally happened! Van Eck reading is a very specialized means of technologically reading a computer's &quot;mind&quot; by examining the EM waves released by it. Even TEMPEST-hardened computers are vulnerable to this, since it isn't &quot;hacking&quot; in a conventional sense. It's undetectable, but needs hefty equipment (unless you're doing it with magick, of course). However, Van Eck is a read-only maneuver... unless you understand Enlightened Programming Procedures. This maneuver can only be learnt if you already possess 3 dots in the Technology Skill, and it allows a hacker to give input to a computer through the input of certain wavelengths and frequencies, reverse-engineering Van Eck Reading.<br /> <br /> Roll Intelligence + EP as though you were performing a typical Computer maneuver, but increase the difficulty by 3. The main upshot of using this maneuver is that the input comes &quot;from out of nowhere&quot; leaving no mundane traces, does not require a traditional means of access (like a terminal) and overrides all conventional (and most unconventional) means of protecting a computer. It does, however, require specialized and heavy equipment; a small kit would work over a small distance, and a specially equipped van with a dish array could perform the trick from a few hundred meters away.<br /> <br /> - Secure Server.<br /> <br /> The computers you build, and the programs you create, are automatically hardened against cracking and hacking. All attempts (mundane or otherwise) to subvert your systems or exploit them are made at +2 difficulty.<br /> <br /> - Enlightened Efficiency.<br /> <br /> When you are using a system, you can speed it up and heighten its efficiency by turning off unnecessary programs and executables, restructuring memory and optimizing the system's handling of the programs you are focusing on. The means may be normal, but the results are exceptional; any computer you are using will be able to handle Sphere effects up to Level 3, not 2, without the need to &quot;harden&quot; the system to allow for complex magickal effects (which would otherwise slow them down or damage their hardware). Furthermore, any penalties imposed by using a slow or outdated PC may be ignored, at least in the short term (eventually the hardware is going to give).<br /> <br /> - Signal Boost.<br /> <br /> Your enhanced understanding of blutooth, WiFi, mobile data and phone signal allow you to stretch the limits of acquiring digital information juuust a bit further (or quite a lot further) than everyone else. You may roll your Perception + EP at a difficulty of 3 to 9 (difficulty 3 being &quot;why the hell doesn't this place have 4G&quot; or &quot;come on I'm in the garden, the internet should work out here&quot; and difficulty 9 being reserved for moderately ludicrous applications, such as having the phone signal to call for emergency services in the middle of a huge desert); success will grant you the access you need.<br /> <br /> - Routed Work.<br /> <br /> It's second nature for you to do all of your online work &quot;through, like, 5 different servers in 5 different countries!&quot; as many films aptly put it. To a determined Virtual Adept, your fingerprint is still traceable, but otherwise you are a ghost. This maneuver represents the innate advantage given by your mastery of Enlightened Programming; this is a realistic precaution which is much less cumbersome for you personally thanks to some heightened reality.<br /> <br /> All attempts to trace your online or digital fingerprint, gain your IP or follow activity back to your computer/handle are at +2 difficulty. If the optional Data Sphere is being used, then the strength of connection needed to effect you will be 2 degrees higher than normal (much to the chagrin of those who use the ability; expect no mercy once they get their hands on you).<br /> <br /> - Buying Time.<br /> <br /> You can &quot;shock&quot; a system's defenses with the code equivalent of an EMP; an attempted soft reset for everyone but you in a server which leaves moderators, rival programmers and anti-virus AI &quot;confused&quot;. This effect will not discriminate between intended and unintended targets. When used in the Digital Web, this maneuver is incredibly obnoxious and will win you many enemies.<br /> <br /> Once per scene you may spend a point of Willpower and roll your Intelligence + EP, difficulty 6. Each success reduces the dicepool of other characters (AI, defensive programmers) in the scene by 1, until the end of the next round.<br /> <br /> If this roll is Botched in the Digital Web, then the resulting White-Out will Soft De-Rez the user immediately.<br /> <br /> - sixthsense.exe<br /> <br /> Your ally's email got hacked. Was it a magical infiltration by a VA? The Technocracy? Or did someone just... you know... hack their email? An Enlightened Practitioner gains a sense of what is mundane (regular cracking) and what is abnormal (enlightened procedures) within digital spaces.<br /> <br /> The programmer may roll Perception + Awareness in online and computerized spaces to determine if what they are observing is the result of typical Computing, Enhanced Programming, or a supernaturally enhanced effect (Sphere Magick, Technothaumaturgy, Glass Walker Gifts, mischievous Tech Spirits). A single success will only divide the mundane from the supernatural (this handle seems normal, this user seems unusual), while multiple successes will give more details, in terms that a user comprehends and already understands (I get the feeling that this post is a memetic hazard created using psychodynamics (Mind), I get the sense that this user is manipulating tech spirits to enhance his hacking abilities).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 04-30-2018, 07:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T07:20:58-07:00","id":1212263,"title":"","content":"Neat, I like the idea of mages having cuasi-magical &quot;skills&quot; that are better than their mundane counterparts as an extension of their craft. After all, if Akashicks can DO it... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Another one that can't fail:<br /> <br /> -Fast Typing.<br /> Everyone knows that if you let a hacker alone with a computer half a minute he can control all systems of a building. With fingers flashing trough the keyboard a hacker can fight against a virus or create one in no time.<br /> Having this technique halves the time required to do any computer related roll when you're using a keyboard or another analog input device and eliminates any stress-based penalty accrued for having to work under unrealistic time constraints. Also, this eliminates the &quot;fast casting&quot; penalty when these devices are used as Instrument - the character it's as trained to use it's knowledge under presure as combat mages are trained to use their own skills.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Enlightened Efficiency.<br /> <br /> When you are using a system, you can speed it up and heighten its efficiency by turning off unnecessary programs and executables, restructuring memory and optimizing the system's handling of the programs you are focusing on. The means may be normal, but the results are exceptional; any computer you are using will be able to handle Sphere effects up to Level 3, not 2, without the need to &quot;harden&quot; the system to allow for complex magickal effects (which would otherwise slow them down or damage their hardware). Furthermore, any penalties imposed by using a slow or outdated PC may be ignored, at least in the short term (eventually the hardware is going to give).</div> </div> </div> </div>While I do like this idea a lot (after all, running Doom in a toaster it's an ongoing joke among IT circles), I have a cruzade against the idea that non-trinary computers &quot;can't handle&quot; spells above Sphere level 2.<br /> <br /> Why?<br /> <br /> 1. No other Instrument has that penalty. You don't need a Trinary Camera to run NWO surveilance of any level. You don't need a Phoenix Feather inserted in your wand because normal wood explodes when you use it to cast a fireball. NO other focus has this &quot;exotic ingredient&quot; prerequisite to evolve beyond lvl.2 effects - why punish computer users?, Why can't the authors reinforce the tropes they like trough &quot;positive&quot; interaction (like giving a bonus because you're using an exotic Wonder-like Instrument)?.<br /> <br /> 2. The worst it's that among programming circles, the idea of optimizing a program so it needs less resources it's regarded as an elite skill. I knew hackers that came from poor families, and they remember things like making a working computer from trash with pride. However, VA have the most wasteful Focus of all Mage. They <i>need </i>a bizarre &quot;Wonder&quot; that you don't know how to build and it's supposed to be expensive as shit. That's lame. And VA are Lame because of that.<br /> <br /> 3. Also, since VA existed since the telegraph, I'm left to believe that either:<ul><li>These ancient VA had &quot;trinary telegraphs&quot;.</li> <li>These ancient VA died Apprentices</li> <li>VA technology devolved into needing more resources to do the same mojo. It seems that, the more advanced the Instrument, the worse it works</li> </ul>Nah. I'm not indulging any those limitations just because the authors are obsessed with a few tropes. It would be like to force Hermetics to wear balck robes and Choristers to wear white priest robes. I'm not doing that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 04-27-2018, 10:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T07:35:18-07:00","id":1212268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1212010-enlightened-programming?p=1212263#post1212263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Neat, I like the idea of mages having cuasi-magical &quot;skills&quot; that are better than their mundane counterparts as an extension of their craft. After all, if Akashicks can DO it... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Another one that can't fail:<br /> <br /> -Fast Typing.<br /> Everyone knows that if you let a hacker alone with a computer half a minute he can control all systems of a building. With fingers flashing trough the keyboard a hacker can fight against a virus or create one in no time.<br /> Having this technique halves the time required to do any computer related roll when you're using a keyboard or another analog input device and eliminates any stress-based penalty accrued for having to work under unrealistic time constraints. Also, this eliminates the &quot;fast casting&quot; penalty when these devices are used as Instrument - the character it's as trained to use it's knowledge under presure as combat mages are trained to use their own skills.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> While I do like this idea a lot (after all, running Doom in a toaster it's an ongoing joke among IT circles), I have a cruzade against the idea that non-trinary computers &quot;can't handle&quot; spells above Sphere level 2.<br /> <br /> Why?<br /> <br /> 1. No other Instrument has that penalty. You don't need a Trinary Camera to run NWO surveilance of any level. You don't need a Phoenix Feather inserted in your wand because normal wood explodes when you use it to cast a fireball. NO other focus has this &quot;exotic ingredient&quot; prerequisite to evolve beyond lvl.2 effects - why punish computer users?, Why can't the authors reinforce the tropes they like trough &quot;positive&quot; interaction (like giving a bonus because you're using an exotic Wonder-like Instrument)?.<br /> <br /> 2. The worst it's that among programming circles, the idea of optimizing a program so it needs less resources it's regarded as an elite skill. I knew hackers that came from poor families, and they remember things like making a working computer from trash with pride. However, VA have the most wasteful Focus of all Mage. They <i>need </i>a bizarre &quot;Wonder&quot; that you don't know how to build and it's supposed to be expensive as shit. That's lame. And VA are Lame because of that.<br /> <br /> 3. Also, since VA existed since the telegraph, I'm left to believe that either:<ul><li>These ancient VA had &quot;trinary telegraphs&quot;.</li> <li>These ancient VA died Apprentices</li> <li>VA technology devolved into needing more resources to do the same mojo. It seems that, the more advanced the Instrument, the worse it works</li> </ul>Nah. I'm not indulging any those limitations just because the authors are obsessed with a few tropes. It would be like to force Hermetics to wear balck robes and Choristers to wear white priest robes. I'm not doing that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nice idea with speed typing.<br /> <br /> The in-universe justification is that complex magick slows down computers the same way complicated programs do. I feel like the mechanical limitation is in place since Reality Hacking and Everything is Data lead to a lot of flexibility (which many paradigms have) and a lot of coincidence (which many paradigms have). The problem is that when your focus allows for tonnes of flexibility and gives you access to nearly all sphere effects (&quot;I can change anything through hacking&quot; leaves more room for different effects than &quot;God's will allows me to perform miracles&quot;), and when your focus makes many of those effects coincidental (hacking all of a person's transactions and online activity is coincidental, and achieves the same result as figuring out that they have committed a crime by a deep reading of their mind, which will often be vulgar), that can be a dangerous combination.<br /> <br /> So requiring reinforced computers for level 3, and trinary computers for 4+, is probably an attempt at balancing things out.<br /> <br /> What will have happened is that the VAs found that computers had incredible potential for unenlightened work, but their inherent complexity meant that working magick through them wasn't simple at higher ranks. This will have left Masters using level 1-3 effects through simple computers and the nascent internet, and channeling their more powerful effects through other means, the ones they used before computers.<br /> <br /> However your complaints makes a TONNE of sense and honestly I'm less comfortable with the rule than I was before.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T08:42:58-07:00","id":1212302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I feel like the mechanical limitation is in place since Reality Hacking and Everything is Data lead to a lot of flexibility (which many paradigms have) and a lot of coincidence (which many paradigms have). The problem is that when your focus allows for tonnes of flexibility and gives you access to nearly all sphere effects (&quot;I can change anything through hacking&quot; leaves more room for different effects than &quot;God's will allows me to perform miracles&quot;), and when your focus makes many of those effects coincidental (hacking all of a person's transactions and online activity is coincidental, and achieves the same result as figuring out that they have committed a crime by a deep reading of their mind, which will often be vulgar), that can be a dangerous combination. </div> </div> </div>While you may think that (and that's what the book say, after all), it often doesn't. Use of Focus it's a creative exercise on part of the player and the ST, it's hard to determine what a Focus can or can't do . Saavy players will hide their mystical practice, while players that aren't that saavy will use ultra-tech in such an overt maner that they will gather Paradox anyway.<br /> <br /> Praying to bless your shotgun it's as effective as praying to summon fire form the heavens - and doing the same with reality-hacking it's no less Vulgar/Coincident AND needs a physical tool (good thing you always have your trinary cellphone on you, isn't it?). Of course, you can &quot;reality-hack&quot; to shut down the lights of a building, but praying so &quot;God gives you an opportunity&quot; can also cause a Coincident blackout because blackouts do happen (you don't need to literally ask God to shut down the lights, HE knows what to do).<br /> <br /> Now, if security cameras already caught your image, I can see magickally hacking them to erase the data as being Coincident while praying for the data to be erased would be Vulgar - because it's laser focused on a Mythic Thread (Data doesn't just vanish, unless someone touches a computer, that's it). But, on the other hand, in some Reality Zones faith healing may be Coincident whereas &quot;reality-hacking&quot; would have a lot of problems pulling that &quot;milacre&quot; even in Silicon Valley.<br /> <br /> No magick that cannot possibly be seen by mortals will ever be Vulgar unless it directly contradicts Earthly Foundations big time. Mind reading it's always Coincident unless you make the effort to prove the sleeper beyond reasonable doubt that you're, indeed, reading his mind (That I don't know how the fuck do you know my real name doesn't mean that I believe you're a literal wizard).<br /> <br /> Point being, that advantage it's debatable and ultimately depends a lot on Player's imagination and knowledge","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 04-27-2018, 11:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}